/* Authored mascot frames: trash, the head-first dive into the Trash can, drawn by hand so the OS does not rotate the canvas with CSS (rotate() tears the pixels).
   Format: lintPoseFrames in tools/lint_mascot_body.mjs; tools/lint_anim_trash.mjs has the extra rules. Drawn with compose({pose:'trash:<i>', flip:0|1, air:1}) (os.js trashPose).

   HOW THEY ARE DRAWN. The whole character (T2 stretch body, the 'together' shoes, the two nubs, the stem and the stage-3 leaf) turns CLOCKWISE about the T2 body
   centre (19.6, 43.7) and is redrawn: a clean 1 px outline on the turned silhouette, the light kept in the world (p highlight on the upper-left slope, R shade on the
   right and underside), the shoes re-placed by hand (behind the body, only the visible parts drawn). The nubs are mascot/arms.js buckets attached the way compose attaches
   them (a ray from the turned T2 ctr at the bucket angle, anchor snapped to the outline): 0 [210,330] (= compose), 1 [210,300], 2 [120,240], 3 [60,210], 4..6 [30,150], 7 [0,150]. Every frame is baked:true: v = the body (k r p R
   only), over = shoes, nubs, stem, leaf, face, cheeks and sweat bead; compose adds no face, sprout, hat, arms or cheeks. face:[x0,y0,x1,y1] is the box the baked face
   lies in (compose ignores it; the lint checks the face sits on body fill with a clear 1 px ring).
   He is WORRIED (he is being thrown away): wide-open 6x7 eyes, thin brows a clear row above them slanting up toward the middle, a small wobbly mouth, cheeks, and in
   frames 0..3 a teal sweat bead beside the head. The face turns with the body: at 90 and 180 degrees it is an exact turn of the upright face; at 45 and 135 the eye
   boxes stay upright and the brows, mouth and pupils are placed on the turned face. Upside down the brows are under the eyes and the mouth above them.

   FRAMES (index: pose; canvas rows: body / everything)
     0  ready: upright T2, shoes together, nubs down, leaf up; pupils down toward the can. Pixel for pixel compose({lv:'T2',ft:'together',stage:3}) apart from
        the face and the bead, so swapping into it does not jump.                                                                   body 28..57 / 17..59
     1  ~45 degrees: head up-right; the shoes trail (still upright, hanging down-left), the leaf flops back over the head; pupils down.  body 32..57 / 23..63
     2  ~90 degrees, on his side, head right: shoes tucked against his back (soles out), leaf flung up behind the head tip.          body 33..54 / 28..57
     3  ~135 degrees, head down-right: shoes up and to the left, leaf trailing up the right side.                                     body 31..57 / 25..57
     4  180 degrees, upside down, diving, KICK A: his world-left shoe kicked straight up (toe up), the other flat, sole up.           body 29..58 / 20..63
     5  180 degrees, KICK B: the other way round (world-right shoe up).                                                               body 29..58 / 21..63
     6  rummage tilt ~170 degrees (body leaning one way, both shoes flat, the right one higher).                                     body 29..58 / 24..63
     7  rummage tilt ~190 degrees (lopsided the other way, the left shoe higher; not a mirror of 6).                                  body 29..57 / 24..62
     8..11  the same four seen from BEHIND (4, 5, 6, 7 with the face, cheeks, worried look and the arm nubs gone), used for the rummage inside the can. The body has a little
        crack at the shoe end (the top edge of the body, between the shoes): 4 px of outline in the over layer, curving one column over.
   Upside down (4..7) the HEAD is at the BOTTOM: shoes rows 20..34, belly 29..45, eyes 41..47, head tip 57..58, the leaf hangs under it in rows 59..63.
   The leaf: a stage-3 leaf rotated rigidly does not fit the 40x64 cell from 45 to 180 degrees, so it follows through instead (flops back over the head, flung up
   behind it, trailing up the side) and hangs as a flatter 5-row leaf under the head when upside down.

   WIRING NOTE (os.js; the OS plays poses with setTimeout/anim). Pose looks: {pose:'trash:<i>', flip:<0|1>, air:1} (trashPose). Travelling right flip:0, left flip:1.
   OFFSET. The drawn frames turn about the body centre; the old CSS rotate(180deg) turned the 40x64 canvas about its middle (row y -> 63-y). Upside down the
   drawn body sits EXACTLY 23 art rows LOWER than a CSS-rotated frame 0 would (body rows 29..58 instead of 6..35; centroid row 42.3 instead of 19.3). Every place
   os.js used off=12*bh/48 (the old 32x48 cell) now uses off = 23*bh/64.
   binShow (an icon dragged into the Trash; the mascot rummages):
     - the flip at the end of the third hop (220 ms): frames 0,1,2,3,4 at 44 ms each (as now: i=floor(k*5)), top ramping down by off*k.
     - going in (300 ms) and the rummage: the head is at the BOTTOM of the canvas, so the clip comes up from the bottom edge: top = topIn + d - off,
       clipPath = inset(0 0 max(0, d - off) px 0) (as now, with the new off). Rummage: cycle 8, 10, 9, 11 (kick A, tilt, kick B, tilt, seen from behind; going in switches 4 to 8) at 110 ms each, the 4 px
       sideways wobble on top, for as long as bin.until runs.
     - climbing out: hold 4 while d runs down (220 ms), then for the 380 ms hop to the left play flip:1 frames 3, 2, 1 (and 0) at ~95 ms each (the turn
       carries on past 180 degrees), top = arc - off*(1-k); then the existing stretch/idle play() upright.
   trashDive (the mascot himself dropped on the Trash): drag-dive = flip, then the kicking drop.
     - the slide over the can (150 ms): frame 0. Frames 1 and 4 reach the canvas's last row (a trailing shoe, the hanging leaf), so for an unclipped flip
       above the rim use flipY = rimY - bh (was rimY - bh*46/48).
     - the flip, unclipped (220 ms): 1, 2, 3, 4 at 55 ms; the frames turn in place, so no offset is needed here.
     - the drop (280 ms): 4 and 5 alternating every 90-110 ms with the bottom clip(t) unchanged (the head, at the canvas bottom, goes in first).
   Game (60 Hz): flip 0-4 at 3 steps each; kick 4/5 every 6 steps; rummage 8,10,9,11 (from behind) at 7 steps each; climb out 3,2,1 at 6 steps each (flip:1).
   REDUCED MOTION: neither sequence runs (trashDive drops him, binShow only waits). If one static pose is wanted, use frame 0.

   LIMITS. Baked frames carry no hat (a hat vanishes for the dive and comes back after) and always the stage-3 leaf: a player at leaf stage 0..2 (or 4) sees
   the leaf change for the length of the dive. Frame 0 matches the stage-3 stretch pose; at another stage only the leaf differs on the swap. compose() needs no change. */
